----------------\nTorchiani - Paint & Coatings Italy (https://www.paint-coatings.it/exhibitor/torchiani/)\nciteturn76search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Address: Via Gian Battista Cacciamali, 45, Brescia, 25125, Italy ... The paints and coatings sector is one of our areas of expertise, where we offer high-tech solutions such as colloidal silica, photocatalytic titanium dioxide, and functional additives to enhance durability, resistance, and sustainability.\n\n# Torchiani\n\nImage\n\nStand: 322\n\nFULL LIST OF CATEGORIES:\n\nTelephone: +39 030 3511411\nEmail: info@torchiani.com\nWebsite: https://torchiani.com/\nAddress: Via Gian Battista Cacciamali, 45, Brescia, 25125, Italy\n\n## Company Profile\n\nDal 1928, Torchiani Srl distribuisce materie prime e formulati chimici per l’industria ed è rappresentante di primari produttori internazionali. Il settore pitture e vernici è uno dei nostri ambiti di competenza, dove offriamo soluzioni ad alto contenuto tecnico come silice colloidale, biossido di titanio fotocatalitico e additivi funzionali per migliorare resistenza, durabilità e sostenibilità delle formulazioni. Operiamo anche in altri comparti industriali, garantendo competenza tecnica, reattività e presenza sul territorio. Con oltre 95 anni di esperienza, affianchiamo clienti e partner con un approccio consulenziale e un portafoglio selezionato di prodotti ad alte prestazioni.\n\nSince 1928, Torchiani Srl has been distributing raw materials and chemical formulations and representing leading international manufacturers. The paints and coatings sector is one of our areas of expertise, where we offer high-tech solutions such as colloidal silica, photocatalytic titanium dioxide, and functional additives to enhance durability, resistance, and sustainability. We also serve a wide range of other industrial sectors, providing strong technical expertise, responsiveness, and local presence. With over 95 years of experience, we support customers and partners with a consultative approach and a carefully selected portfolio of high-performance products.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTitanium dioxide (https://www.isprambiente.gov.it/files2024/pubblicazioni/rapporti/nir-2024-r-398-24.pdf)\nciteturn76search12 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2.3 years ago; In Italy there is only one facility where this production occurs and titanium dioxide is produced through the sulphate process.The “sulphate process” involves the use of sulphuric acid to concentrate the input raw mineral in terms of titanium dioxide content, then selective precipitation and calcination allow getting the final product.\nTitanium dioxide\n\nTitanium dioxide (TiO₂) is the most used white pigment especially for paint and plastic industries. As described also in the IPCC Guidelines, two main production routes are available:\n\n- the chloride route, which has both “combustion” and “process” emissions;\n- the sulphate process, whose emissions are only related to the combustion of fuels.\n\nIn Italy there is only one facility where this production occurs and titanium dioxide is produced through the sulphate process. The “sulphate process” involves the use of sulphuric acid to concentrate the input raw mineral in terms of titanium dioxide content, then selective precipitation and calcination allow getting the final product. Main process chemical reactions can be summarized like in the following box:\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nBox with three chemical reactions:\nFeTiO₃ + 2H₂SO₄ → FeSO₄ + TiO.SO₄ + 2H₂O\nTiO.SO₄ + 2H₂O → TiO₂.H₂O + H₂SO₄\nTiO₂.H₂O + heat → TiO₂ + H₂O\n</visual_element>\n\nTherefore, under 2B6 and the notation key “NO” has been reported in the CRF because no process emissions are originated by the sulphate process.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTitanium Dioxide – L'Aprochimide Srl (https://aprochimide.it/titanium-dioxide/?lang=en)\nciteturn76search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; ## Titanium Dioxide ... Why choose L’Aprochimide for the supply of titanium dioxide, anatase and rutile. ... Come materia prima si preferisce il rutilo, minerale che può essere mescolato con coke di petrolio, trasformato in mattonelle con l’ausilio di leganti e trattato con cloro gassoso a 500÷800°.\n\nTitanium dioxide, Anatase and Rutilio distribution by L’Aprochimide\n\nWhy choose L’Aprochimide for the supply of titanium dioxide, anatase and rutile.\n\nCONTACT US\n\nImage\n\n### Bags\n\nAvailable in 25 kg bags\n\nImage\n\n### Big Bags\n\nRUTILE TITANIUM DIOXIDE\nAvailable in Big Bags\n\nImage\n\n### Bulk\n\nTITANIUM DIOXIDE RUTILO\nBulk product delivery\n\n\n# Titanium Dioxide\n\n### CAS\n\n13463-67-7\n\n### EC\n\n236-675-5\n\n### TARIFFA DOGANALE\n\n32.06.1100\n\nAnatase - Rutilo\n\nAll’incirca il 95% del titanio viene consumato in forma di diossido di titanio (TiO2), un pigmento intensamente bianco e permanente con buona capacità coprente, nelle vernici, nella carta, nei cementi per renderli più brillanti e nelle plastiche. Le vernici fatte con il biossido di titanio sono eccellenti riflettrici della radiazione infrarossa e sono quindi usate estensivamente dagli astronomi.A causa della loro resistenza (anche alla corrosione), leggerezza, e capacità di sopportare temperature estreme, le leghe di titanio vengono utilizzate principalmente nell’industria aeronautica e aerospaziale, anche se il loro utilizzo in prodotti di consumo quali: mazze da golf, biciclette, componenti motociclistici e computer portatili, sta diventando sempre più comune. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBrenntag - Paint & Coatings Italy (https://www.paint-coatings.it/exhibitor/brenntag/)\nciteturn76search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Indirizzo: Milanofiori Strada 6, Palazzo A/13, Assago, MI, 20057, Italy ...   * Titanium Dioxide and Pigments\n\nOur extensive product range includes, among others:\n\n  * T